When loading parsed files, validate the parsed file shape, record malformed entry diagnostics, and pass those diagnostics into the package validator to ensure it fails closed. If an expected array field is present but is not an array, record a validation failure and process it as an empty array to prevent TypeErrors.

```javascript
  const rawSourceRows = sourceMapRows(inputs.sourceMap, paths, diagnostics);
  let registryRows = [];
  if (inputs.sourceDocumentRegistry) {
    if (typeof inputs.sourceDocumentRegistry !== 'object' || Array.isArray(inputs.sourceDocumentRegistry)) {
      diagnostics.push({
        code: 'malformed_input_file',
        role: 'question_render_source_document_registry',
        path: paths.sourceDocumentRegistry,
        reason: 'invalid_shape',
        severity: 'critical',
      });
    } else if ('registry' in inputs.sourceDocumentRegistry && !Array.isArray(inputs.sourceDocumentRegistry.registry)) {
      diagnostics.push({
        code: 'malformed_input_file',
        role: 'question_render_source_document_registry',
        path: paths.sourceDocumentRegistry,
        reason: 'registry_is_not_an_array',
        severity: 'critical',
      });
    } else {
      registryRows = inputs.sourceDocumentRegistry.registry || [];
    }
  }
  let cropRiskRows = [];
  if (inputs.historicalCropRiskAudit) {
    if (typeof inputs.historicalCropRiskAudit !== 'object' || Array.isArray(inputs.historicalCropRiskAudit)) {
      diagnostics.push({
        code: 'malformed_input_file',
        role: 'question_render_historical_crop_risk_audit',
        path: paths.historicalCropRiskAudit,
        reason: 'invalid_shape',
        severity: 'critical',
      });
    } else if ('rows' in inputs.historicalCropRiskAudit && !Array.isArray(inputs.historicalCropRiskAudit.rows)) {
      diagnostics.push({
        code: 'malformed_input_file',
        role: 'question_render_historical_crop_risk_audit',
        path: paths.historicalCropRiskAudit,
        reason: 'rows_is_not_an_array',
        severity: 'critical',
      });
    } else {
      cropRiskRows = inputs.historicalCropRiskAudit.rows || [];
    }
  }
  const rows = buildInventoryRows({
    sourceRows: rawSourceRows,
    registryRows,
    cropRiskRows,
    paths,
    generatedAt,
    diagnostics,
  });
```

<details>
<summary>References</summary>

1. When loading parsed files (such as JSON), validate the parsed file shape, record malformed entry diagnostics, skip bad entries, and pass those diagnostics into the package validator to ensure it fails closed.
2. When validating expected array fields in input data, if a field is present but is not an array, record a validation failure (blocker) and process it as an empty array. This prevents TypeErrors during execution while ensuring the system fails closed.
</details>

